      "side": 1,
      "message": "My hypothesis is that removing mem-offline changes the phandle assignments in the DTB. qcom,use-power-supply \u003d \u003c2\u003e is a numeric mode, but fw_devlink interprets it as a supplier phandle because of the -supply suffix.\nWith mem-offline present, phandle 2 may refer to a node whose dependency is satisfied or ignored. Without it phandle 2 resolves to /soc/syscon@1fc0000, leaving FSA4480 waiting for an unavailable supplier. Renaming the property to qcom,use-power-supply-mode in both the DT and driver removes this false dependency and allows the device to boot.",
      "revId": "e41840686a3b4db17d2126685736d8184c315c0f",
      "serverId": "1ec6b3db-b2c1-4fa4-84a2-4c7efe89ba71"
    },
